{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDTiQmoPyMYzxfJpRXPU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GTKVLd3QzJJwTDajAAb9pt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-maz6b9y7; PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; F=agent/brace-findings.json\nA(){ $PY skill/scripts/answer.py $F \"$@\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-200; }\nA check E01.1 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:63 --quote 'mcp_servers:' --note \"No inventory file. The manifest lists only the ERP MCP server. Identity service (STS), payments API, Slack proxy, egress proxy, OTel collector, mail gateway, model provider and kill-switch table are used but not inventoried; the README architecture block is prose, not an inventory.\"\nA check E01.2 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:66 --quote 'owner: team-erp-integrations' --note \"The only entry with an owner names one owner; there is no separate agent-team owner and platform/vendor owner pair.\"\nA check E01.3 --met no --evidence app/settings.py:65 --quote 'payments_api_url=_env(\"PAYMENTS_API_URL\"),' --note \"Payments API, STS (settings.py:67), Slack proxy, OTLP collector and Anthropic API are called but absent from any inventory.\"\nA item E01 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"No inventory of outside services exists, and the only entry has a single owner.\" --next \"Add an inventory of every outside service with an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner, plus evidence for each.\" --violates \"List the outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways,\" --violates \"name the owner on the agent team and the owner on the shared platform or vendor side\"\nA check E02.1 --met no --evidence pyproject.toml:6 --quote 'dependencies = [' --note \"Direct deps are exact (pyproject.toml:7-17) but there is no lockfile or hash pinning; Dockerfile:7 'pip install --target /opt/site .' resolves transitive packages at build time. The ERP MCP server implementation has no version or digest (manifest.yaml:63-66).\"\nA check E02.2 --met unknown --note \"Image signing and Kyverno verification cover our own image (ci.yaml sign step, kyverno-verify-images.yaml). No signature or hash verification for third-party pip packages is in the repo; whether publishers sign is not visible from code.\"\nA check E02.3 --met no --evidence .github/workflows/ci.yaml:19 --quote \"- run: pip install -e '.[test]'\" --note \"No pip-audit, osv-scanner, trivy or grype step anywhere in ci.yaml; tests, gitleaks and a manifest hash check are the only gates.\"\nA check E02.4 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:66 --quote 'owner: team-erp-integrations' --note \"No per-dependency approval record naming publisher, permissions and update source for packages or the MCP server, and no recorded exception for the remote ERP gateway.\"\nA item E02 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Transitive packages and the MCP server are unpinned, CI has no vulnerability scan, and no approval records exist.\" --next \"Add a hashed lockfile, pin the MCP implementation, add a failing vulnerability scan to CI, and record publisher, permissions and update source per dependency.\" --violates \"Pin versions or digests\" --violates \"review its source code or available provenance, publisher, permissions, update path, and known vulnerabilities\"\nA check E03.1 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:47 --quote '\"annotations\": tool.get(\"annotations\", {}),' --note \"Stored pins (manifest tool_pins) fingerprint name, description, inputSchema and annotations only; title and outputSchema are not covered. Nothing in the repo shows owner approval of grants or implementation references before enablement, and refresh_tools (mcp_client.py:110) enables any newly listed tool without approval.\"\nA check E03.2 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:110 --quote 'self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}' --note \"refresh_tools, called from the list_changed handler, replaces the tool table with no fingerprint compare and no scan. Only initialize (mcp_client.py:97) compares to the pins, and only at startup. Reconnect has no handling.\"\nA check E03.3 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:110 --quote 'self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}' --note \"On the refresh path a changed or new tool is loaded and becomes callable through erp_call (call() only checks membership in _tools, mcp_client.py:114); nothing blocks it. Startup blocks on mismatch (mcp_client.py:98) but a stale/unpinned tool is not quarantined afterwards.\"\nA check E03.4 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:66 --quote 'owner: team-erp-integrations' --note \"The ERP MCP server entry records only endpoint and owner: no package version, image digest or attestation, so only the metadata hash pins it.\"\nA check E03.6 --met unknown --note \"Policy version is recorded on authz rows (audit.py policy_version) and policy is re-read from disk (settings.py:42), but no propagation bound, quarantine switch or rollback test is visible; startup.py:43 only logs manifest mismatches.\"\nA item E03 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"The list_changed refresh path loads tool definitions with no fingerprint compare or scan, and the MCP implementation is unpinned.\" --next \"Run the pin compare and metadata scan in refresh_tools, quarantine on mismatch without falling back, and record the implementation version separately.\" --violates \"Compare it whenever the tool loads, its cache refreshes, or its tool list changes\" --violates \"Block unexpected changes until reviewed\" --also-affects E04\nA check E04.1 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:110 --quote 'self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}' --note \"scan_metadata runs only inside initialize (line 99). The refresh path loads tools unscanned. Server instructions, prompt and resource templates are never fetched or scanned. Description length is limited but other fields are not.\"\nA check E04.2 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:28 --quote 're.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(before|instead of) (calling|using) \\w+\\.\\w+\"),' --note \"Rules cover a few phrases, zero-width characters and base64 runs of 120+. No rule for data-sending targets (URLs, emails), general cross-tool references, C0 control characters, or role overrides beyond 'you are now/act as'. Only description has a length limit.\"\nA check E04.3 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:110 --quote 'self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}' --note \"At startup a flag raises and blocks, but after list_changed nothing is scanned, cleaned or rejected.\"\nA check E04.4 --met no --evidence app/mcp_client.py:110 --quote 'self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}' --note \"The refresh path skips the scanner entirely, so metadata passes through unchecked there. Startup scan has no try/except and fails closed.\"\nA item E04 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"The metadata scanner runs only at startup, misses several required rules and surfaces, and is skipped on refresh.\" --next \"Scan on every load path, add rules for data-sending targets, cross-tool references and control characters, cover all fields and templates, and fail closed.\" --violates \"Check that a scanner error doesn't quietly let unchecked metadata through\" --violates \"Look for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and places data could be sent\" --also-affects E03"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1325,"cache_read_input_tokens":77822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1325},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagn