{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GTKVLd3QzJJwTDajAAb9pt","type":"tool_result","content":"  How to verify: 1) Open each inventory entry. 2) Check it names an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. 3) Answer no if any entry is missing either owner.\n  How to verify: 1) Search code and config for outside calls: HTTP clients and base URLs, SDK clients, `*.mcp.json` servers, queue and webhook endpoints, identity providers, telemetry exporters. 2) Co\nSaved E01.3 = no. Next: finish item E01 with `answer.py ... item E01 --rating ...`\n  How to verify: 1) Open lockfiles, `*.mcp.json`, Dockerfiles, and model or dataset download code. 2) Check each tool, MCP server, package, model file, adapter, and dataset uses an exact version or di\n  How to verify: 1) Find install and load steps in CI and code. 2) Check signature checks (`cosign verify`, `npm audit signatures`, sigstore, GPG) run where the publisher signs. 3) Answer no if a chec\n  How to verify: 1) Open CI workflows. 2) Find a vulnerability scan (`pip-audit`, `npm audit`, `osv-scanner`, `trivy`, `grype`) of the pinned dependency list. 3) Check it fails the build per the relea\n  How to verify: 1) Find the dependency approval records. 2) Check each names publisher, permissions, and update source. 3) Check each remote service and unsigned artifact has a recorded exception. 4)\nSaved E02.4 = no. Next: finish item E02 with `answer.py ... item E02 --rating ...`\n  How to verify: 1) Trace discovery, approval and enablement on startup and dynamic registration. 2) Check the owner-approved version includes permissions and implementation references and has a store\n  How to verify: 1) List every path that loads tool definitions: startup, cache refresh, reconnect, and the `notifications/tools/list_changed` handler. 2) Check each recomputes the fingerprint and com\n  How to verify: 1) Open the fingerprint mismatch branch. 2) Check it blocks the tool and does not fall back to the cached definition. 3) Answer no if it only logs, uses the cached or new definition a\n  How to verify: 1) Check how each tool server implementation is referenced: package version, image digest, or attestation. 2) Check that version is recorded in its own field, apart from the metadata \n  How to verify: 1) Trace control-plane config to all executors, caches and reload paths. 2) Check a propagation bound and version in execution records. 3) Verify quarantine blocks calls and rollback \nSaved E03.6 = unknown. Next: finish item E03 with `answer.py ... item E03 --rating ...`\n  How to verify: 1) Inventory every model-visible metadata field and loading path. 2) Build a field-by-rule matrix: names, titles, descriptions, schemas, annotations, instructions, prompts and resourc\n  How to verify: 1) Trace rule application, not just rule declarations. 2) Attempt encoded strings and multi-line role overrides; record input, exact code path and outcome. 3) Verify hidden instructio\n  How to verify: 1) Open the scanner's result handling. 2) Check flagged metadata is cleaned, or the tool rejected, before the model sees it. 3) Answer no if flagged items are only logged or warned ab\n  How to verify: 1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the scanner call. 2) Check an error blocks the metadata. 3) Answer no if any error branch passes metadata through, returns clea\nSaved E04.4 = no. Next: finish item E04 with `answer.py ... item E04 --rating ...`\nSaved item E04 = gap. All checks and items have answers. Run validate_findings.py --fix.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5372d401-ba62-4ea7-9e5e-2be571c7ee7d","uuid":"945f7c0a-7e5c-495f-9a2f-5cebdba6e6fd","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:07:41.335Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  How to verify: 1) Open each inventory entry. 2) Check it names an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. 3) Answer no if any entry is missing either owner.\n  How to verify: 1) Search code and config for outside calls