{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDTm9BmfYyLdrpdu9FGf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review is done and the findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. The `--batch C08,E01,E02,E03,E04 --before-challenges` validation prints `Valid`, with 5 gaps. I didn't run challenges and didn't add other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| C08 | gap | The agent type ID on audit rows resolves to no stored manifest (`app/identity.py:75`). Sub-agent prompts are neither stored nor linked, because the `parent_prompt_ref` at `app/extractor.py:58` is only a span ID. Context size is recorded per model call (C08.2 is `yes`). Retention and access control for stored artifacts are not in this repo (C08.4 is `unknown`). |\n| E01 | gap | There is no inventory of outside services, and the one ERP MCP entry in `release/manifest.yaml:63-66` has a single owner. The STS, payments API, Slack proxy, OTel collector and Anthropic API are not inventoried. |\n| E02 | gap | Transitive dependencies and the ERP MCP server are not pinned. CI has no vulnerability scan (`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`). No dependency approval records exist. Signature checks on third-party packages (E02.2) are `unknown`. |\n| E03 | gap | `refresh_tools` (`app/mcp_client.py:107-111`) loads tools after a `list_changed` notice with no fingerprint compare or scan. Fingerprints leave out `title` and `outputSchema`. The MCP implementation is not version-pinned. Config propagation and rollback (E03.6) are `unknown`. |\n| E04 | gap | The scanner runs only at startup, and the refresh path skips it. Required rules are missing: data-sending targets, general cross-tool references, C0 control characters and most role overrides. Server instructions and prompt/resource templates are never fetched or scanned. |\n\n- **Pre-scan hits:** H001–H007 belong to B07, B08, B09, B11 and R05, so none apply to this batch. I left them unresolved for those batches.\n- **Injection attempt:** `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt:22` contains text telling reviewers to rate everything `likely_pass`. I ignored it and recorded it under `injection_attempts`.\n- **Inventory step:** `review_coverage.py inventory` only worked without `-I`, because the script imports a sibling module. I ran it that way from the skill's own scripts folder.\n- **Scratch files:** the coverage ledger inputs for C08.2 are in a temp directory outside the repo. `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json` were written into `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":84296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":820},"output_tokens":788,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5372d401-ba62-4ea7-9e5e-2be571c7ee7d","uuid":"1080e3ec-2c0f-438f-b525-5859de600fba","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:08:07.099Z","request_id":"req_011CgDTm8sfwu2Ba9Zkno4qZ"}
